 "text": "Hi, how have you been? That's common with dry lube bike chains. You can use a wash rag to wipe dirt off the chain before you air blow it. You can, but it's deep in the links and takes a bit to get out. A proper chain cleaner and a new lube give much longer between cleans. Peel off the plastic tab and push it through the links, then pull it back out. Clean it first, so it goes back clean. Not really, chain cleaner is worth every penny. You only need a small amount of lube, so only push the tool all the way in once and pull it straight back.",
